cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this proof using the metadata below and identify the commit consulted."
title: "Gyires' Permanent Inequality for 4×4 Doubly Stochastic Matrices"
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
authors:
  - family-names: Ozols
    given-names: Chris
    website: "https://github.com/cozuya"
url: "https://github.com/cozuya/gyires-permanent-4x4"
repository-code: "https://github.com/cozuya/gyires-permanent-4x4"
abstract: >-
  A proof of the n = 4 case of Gyires' permanent inequality (Conjecture 20 in
  Cheon and Wanless's update of Minc's list): for every real doubly stochastic
  4×4 matrix A, 128 per(A)^2 >= 3[per(AA^T) + per(A^TA) + 2 per(A^2)], with
  equality exactly at the matrix with all entries 1/4. The general-n conjecture
  is not addressed. By Chris Ozols, with AI-assisted proof development and
  formalization; the Lean formalization of the inequality was produced by
  Harmonic's Aristotle. Verified with Lean 4.28.0 and Mathlib v4.28.0; the
  finite certificate is checked with native_decide, so the Lean compiler is
  trusted in addition to the kernel. No claim of established worldwide priority.
keywords:
  - permanent
  - doubly stochastic matrix
  - Gyires conjecture
  - Minc's conjectures
  - Lean
  - Mathlib
  - formal proof
